sections.original_requirement:
This task must attempt to SOLVE AND CLOSE the entire shared Anthropic-compatible stream architecture in one MAIN task.

Do NOT stop and return to the user merely because:
- a local test fails;
- a reviewer rejects;
- a generated transition cell fails;
- a byte/chunk fault seed fails;
- reload/live continuation diverges;
- an owner mismatch is found;
- capture completeness regresses;
- Strict L3 reports an in-domain warning;
- an isolated suite finds another same-domain defect;
- a larger internal refactor is needed.

Those are work items inside this task. MAIN must use its own engineering judgment, modify the response-side architecture, add regression coverage, rerun proof, and continue until closure or a TRUE non-recoverable boundary is reached.

The target is:
SHARED_ANTHROPIC_STREAM_ARCHITECTURE_CLOSED=YES

After that, if all later gates pass, continue automatically to remaining probes 03-08, Capacity closure, Exact READY dry-run, 13K/20K/30K, Strict L3, and exactly ONE real Full Short.

Last fully reported committed baseline HEAD:
79a99a58ebe95b2be4d1e51a8d190070a2568574

Last sealed architecture-stop facts before the abandoned V3 MAIN:
- worktree dirty by design;
- 68 in-scope changes preserved;
- 3 source-confirmed test side effects preserved;
- memory/narrative-contract.json preserved at its original SHA;
- semantic state/event slice: 11 states x 16 event classes = 176 registered cells;
- 176/176 registered transition tests passed;
- full fault campaign remained INCOMPLETE;
- post-terminal timeout downgrade count = 1;
- post-terminal cancellation downgrade count = 1;
- generic incomplete-terminal replacement count = 4;
- shared protocol regression count = 4;
- Provider-error-lost-to-later-timeout count = 0;
- AttributeError from SSE error payload count = 0;
- post-terminal error ignored count = 0;
- historical exact replay regression count = 0;
- probe-01 exact replay PASS;
- probe-02 exact replay PASS;
- probe-02 usage = 137304 input / 64 output;
- probe-02 ignored post-terminal ping count = 3;
- request identity six-way zero diff;
- prior architecture review had 3 rejects / 2 passes;
- Strict L3 unresolved;
- Capacity NOT_RECOMPUTED;
- real external calls = 0;
- real Full Short = 0;
- sealed external root: C:\小说\cw-final-stop-v1

The abandoned V3 MAIN may have made additional local changes. Recover exact current truth; do not assume no progress occurred.

Do not restart from zero. For each area classify current state as ABSENT / PARTIAL / COMPLETE_UNVERIFIED / COMPLETE_VERIFIED:
- raw/framing state machine;
- semantic reducer;
- durable-prefix contract;
- single durable owner;
- Full Short observer ack alignment;
- rehydration/restart;
- causal precedence;
- generated transition tests;
- byte/chunk fault campaign;
- Full Short observer integration;
- historical exact replay;
- request zero-diff;
- isolated related suite;
- isolated full suite;
- independent review;
- Strict L3.

Do not recreate work already present.

Do not keep critical execution state only in the conversation.
Create an external/non-Git takeover ledger, preferably:
C:\小说\shared-anthropic-v4-takeover-ledger\
(or another source-grounded external path if unavailable).

After every major closure-loop iteration persist:
- timestamp;
- current HEAD;
- worktree manifest/hash;
- architecture decision summary;
- closed findings;
- open findings;
- test/replay/fault/reviewer status;
- child-agent conclusions;
- next local action;
- real external-call counters;
- freeze status.

This ledger must make future context compaction non-fatal.

Any related/full suite capable of mutating the repo must run only in an isolated byte-identical source copy.
Procedure:
1 hash original source;
2 create isolated copy;
3 verify byte identity;
4 run suite in isolation;
5 save logs/receipts;
6 hash original again;
7 prove original was untouched.

Final targets:
ISOLATED_SUITE_SOURCE_IDENTITY=PASS
ORIGINAL_REPO_MUTATION_FROM_ISOLATED_SUITE_COUNT=0

If isolation itself is defective, fix it and rerun. Do not stop on first isolation failure.

Converge to exactly ONE authoritative owner of durable stream progress and terminal truth.

Target architecture may use different names but must be equivalent to:
RAW BYTE INGESTION
 -> INCREMENTAL SSE FRAMER
 -> NORMALIZED EVENT DECODER
 -> SEMANTIC REDUCER
 -> SINGLE DURABLE STREAM OWNER
      -> DURABLE CHECKPOINT
      -> FULL SHORT OBSERVER ACK
      -> REHYDRATION / RESTART
      -> FINAL TYPED RESULT

The durable owner must persist enough information to determine:
- highest durable raw prefix;
- highest complete framed-event prefix;
- highest semantically accepted prefix;
- pending partial-frame state where required;
- semantic success terminal identity;
- Provider-error terminal identity;
- terminal-evidence durability;
- post-terminal tail diagnostics;
- restart/resume cursor;
- rehydrated state;
- final-result eligibility.

Final invariants:
DURABLE_STREAM_OWNER_COUNT=1
OWNER_MISMATCH_COUNT=0
FULL_SHORT_OBSERVER_AND_SHARED_OWNER_CONSISTENT=YES
DURABLE_ACK_SEMANTICS_UNAMBIGUOUS=YES

Distinguish equivalents of:
RAW_DURABLE_PREFIX
FRAMED_EVENT_DURABLE_PREFIX
SEMANTIC_ACCEPTED_PREFIX
TERMINAL_EVENT_IDENTITY
TERMINAL_EVIDENCE_DURABLE
TAIL_DIAGNOSTIC_PROGRESS

Invariants:
1 durable raw progress never moves backward;
2 framed-event durable progress never moves backward;
3 semantic accepted progress never moves backward;
4 durably proven success cannot be revoked by later tail framing/timeout/cancel;
5 durably proven Provider error cannot be replaced by later tail framing/timeout/cancel;
6 partial frame after durable terminal belongs to tail diagnostics;
7 partial frame before terminal may block completion;
8 terminal identity is immutable after durable commit except under an explicit source-grounded fatal rule.

Define one explicit durable ack contract:
- acknowledgement unit;
- owner;
- emit point;
- persistence transaction boundary;
- observer semantics;
- restart semantics;
- tail persistence;
- final-result eligibility.

If the observer uses incompatible legacy return values, migrate it in this task.

Final:
DURABLE_STREAM_OWNER_COUNT=1
OWNER_MISMATCH_COUNT=0
FULL_SHORT_OBSERVER_AND_SHARED_OWNER_CONSISTENT=YES
DURABLE_ACK_SEMANTICS_UNAMBIGUOUS=YES

For every persistable state:
LIVE_CONTINUATION_RESULT = RELOAD_THEN_CONTINUE_RESULT
for identical remaining input.

Test at least:
- before message_start;
- mid-content;
- after usage update;
- partial frame before terminal if persisted;
- after Provider error durable commit;
- after message_stop durable commit;
- terminal + ping;
- terminal + partial ping;
- terminal + timeout diagnostic;
- terminal + cancellation diagnostic.

Final:
REHYDRATION_STATE_COVERAGE=100_PERCENT_REGISTERED_PERSISTABLE_STATES
RELOAD_CONTINUATION_DIVERGENCE_COUNT=0
TAIL_STATE_RELOAD_GAP_COUNT=0

If state is missing, add/migrate it and rerun.

Inject timeout/cancel/EOF/transport faults at raw byte/chunk boundaries including:
- before event field;
- inside event field;
- inside data payload;
- before newline;
- between CR/LF where relevant;
- before blank-line delimiter;
- immediately after complete message_stop;
- inside post-terminal ping;
- after Provider error;
- arbitrary UTF-8-safe chunk boundaries.

Final:
BYTE_BOUNDARY_FAULT_COVERAGE=100_PERCENT_GENERATED_POINTS

Persist every failing seed into the regression corpus. Fix same-domain failures and rerun until green.

After each implementation round:
1 focused tests;
2 generated framing/semantic/durability/rehydration tests;
3 byte/chunk fault campaign;
4 Full Short observer integration;
5 historical replay;
6 isolated related/full suites as appropriate;
7 fresh independent reviewers;
8 update external closure ledger.

If any VALID in-scope finding fails:
- classify it;
- identify owning layer;
- update architecture/implementation;
- add regression fixture;
- rerun impacted proof;
- repeat.

Do NOT return to user for ordinary local findings.
Use engineering judgment. Larger internal refactor is allowed within this response-side domain.
